{"id": "eshop-stock-confirmed-consumer", "repo": "eshop", "shape": "topic", "scope": "cross-service", "query": "which service reacts to the event saying an order's stock was confirmed", "expect_file": "src/Ordering.API/Application/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStockConfirmedIntegrationEventHandler.cs", "expect_symbol": "Handle", "expect_line": 8, "anchor": "public async Task Handle(OrderStockConfirmedIntegrationEvent @event)", "alt_files": [], "expect_related": ["src/Catalog.API/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStatusChangedToAwaitingValidationIntegrationEventHandler.cs"], "why": "Catalog.API constructs OrderStockConfirmedIntegrationEvent at src/Catalog.API/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStatusChangedToAwaitingValidationIntegrationEventHandler.cs:29 and publishes it at :32; Ordering.API subscribes at src/Ordering.API/Extensions/Extensions.cs:56 and this handler at :8 is the only one. The routing key is the event type name (src/EventBusRabbitMQ/RabbitMQEventBus.cs:33), so each project holds its own copy of the event class and the contract is the name."}
{"id": "eshop-stock-confirmed-publisher", "repo": "eshop", "shape": "topic", "scope": "cross-service", "query": "which service publishes the event that confirms the stock for an order", "expect_file": "src/Catalog.API/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStatusChangedToAwaitingValidationIntegrationEventHandler.cs", "expect_symbol": "Handle", "expect_line": 32, "anchor": "await catalogIntegrationEventService.PublishThroughEventBusAsync(confirmedIntegrationEvent);", "alt_files": [], "expect_related": ["src/Ordering.API/Application/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStockConfirmedIntegrationEventHandler.cs"], "why": "Catalog.API checks the stock in the handler at :9, builds the confirmed event at :29 and publishes it at :32 through CatalogIntegrationEventService, whose eventBus.PublishAsync sits at src/Catalog.API/IntegrationEvents/CatalogIntegrationEventService.cs:18; the consumer is Ordering.API. This is the publishing side of eshop-stock-confirmed-consumer."}
{"id": "eshop-price-changed-consumer", "repo": "eshop", "shape": "topic", "scope": "cross-service", "query": "which service subscribes to catalog product price changes", "expect_file": "src/Webhooks.API/IntegrationEvents/ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEventHandler.cs", "expect_symbol": "Handle", "expect_line": 5, "anchor": "public Task Handle(ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEvent @event)", "alt_files": [], "expect_related": ["src/Catalog.API/Apis/CatalogApi.cs"], "why": "src/Catalog.API/Apis/CatalogApi.cs:350 builds ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEvent and :356 publishes it; src/Webhooks.API/Extensions/Extensions.cs:21 holds the only AddSubscription for it and this handler at :5 is the only implementation in the solution."}
{"id": "eshop-orders-table-reader", "repo": "eshop", "shape": "table", "scope": "cross-service", "query": "which service reads the ordering orders table with raw sql instead of going through the ordering api", "expect_file": "src/OrderProcessor/Services/GracePeriodManagerService.cs", "expect_symbol": "GetConfirmedGracePeriodOrders", "expect_line": 71, "anchor": "FROM ordering.orders", "alt_files": [], "expect_related": ["src/Ordering.Infrastructure/EntityConfigurations/OrderEntityTypeConfiguration.cs"], "why": "The table belongs to Ordering: src/Ordering.Infrastructure/EntityConfigurations/OrderEntityTypeConfiguration.cs:7 maps it and src/Ordering.Infrastructure/OrderingContext.cs:37 sets the ordering schema. OrderProcessor opens the same database directly — src/eShop.AppHost/Program.cs:48 wires orderingdb into order-processor — and queries it at GracePeriodManagerService.cs:71, inside GetConfirmedGracePeriodOrders at :63."}

